 "unfinished": {
  "_note": "Is a question finished? (site 2.9, 17 November 2026. The senior author typed 'can i die from ' and was told 'We have no answer to this. Pharmakon answers questions about drugs': 'it should understand and correctly diagnose every instance and meaning of human language'.) By its words alone, the same on the page (insUnfinished) and in the build (Ranker.unfinished), with each drug's name read as 'it'. A question is NOT finished when: (ends) its last word is one a question cannot end on ('can i die from', 'weed and', 'what is the best way to'); (bare) it names a drug, or is asked on a drug's page, and holds nothing but words of 'aux' ('is cocaine', 'how does mdma'); (which) it names no drug, is not asked on a drug's page, and every word is in 'aux', 'func' or 'topic' ('is it addictive', 'can you overdose', 'how long does it last': what it is about has not been said), unless it has no word of 'gap' and holds a word of 'nouns', or begins with 'why' and holds a word of 'topic' ('how long does withdrawal last', 'why do people get addicted': general questions); (typing) its last word is not a word (not in the model's vocabulary, not in these lists, not a known word without its ending) and is the beginning of a drug's name ('can i die from coc') or, in a question that otherwise reads as one about drugs, of a word of these lists ('is weed lega'). 'strand': patterns of questions that may end on such a word ('what are pills cut with', 'what is a comedown like'); 'whole': patterns of questions that are finished all the same ('what is tolerance', 'who are you'). Two drugs' names joined by words of 'join' are a finished question ('weed and alcohol'); 'named': patterns that are finished when the 'it' is a drug's name ('what is ketamine', 'what is ketamine for'). A question that is not finished gets no verdict and no way to send it: the page asks which drug is meant, or to go on, and shows the nearest answers; scripts/auto/ask.py never lists one. Measured by scripts/insight/build_index.py --words (no model needed): how many real forum questions the rule wrongly calls unfinished, and how many questions cut off before the drug's name it catches.",
